{
  "id": "nested-checked-record-ruby-ordinary-full-installed",
  "kind": "installed",
  "revision": "6d0c683e2da19cd6216384ff588294951af216db",
  "command": "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_GEM='/app/.toolchains/ruby33/bin/gem' LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_TEST_GLIBC_FLOOR='2.36' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_RUBY_MAX_LOAD='20' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_RUBY_MODES='full,result-only' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_RUBY_OUTPUT='/app/build/vo1508-nested-record-ruby-6d0c683-archive/records' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_RUBY_ROUTES='ordinary,reviewed' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_RUBY_TEST='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_RUBY='/app/.toolchains/ruby33/bin/ruby' LEAN_NUM_THREADS='1' OMP_NUM_THREADS='1' MAKEFLAGS='-j1' 'taskset' '-c' '3' 'nice' '-n' '10' 'node' '--test' '--test-concurrency=1' '--test-reporter=tap' 'tests/helpers/nested-checked-record-ruby-installed-tests.mjs'",
  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce the complete native gem. Author roots are removed before offline installation; the unchanged caller runs before and after moving the complete installed tree, giving two executions per selection. The full API checks direct and repeated parameters, Array, List, Option, Product, both Except branches, Holder.packet and the active Choice::Packet.value field, including exact per-site constructors, normalization, complete rejected-input snapshots and recovery. Checked-record Ruby acceptance covers the established top-level Interval, Sized 3 and Bounded 0 101 forms plus the tested acyclic Packet, Holder and Choice forms through Array, List, Option, Product and Except copied positions. Generic, recursive and inherited checked records, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete native gems from two author roots, remove author roots, install offline, and replay the unchanged caller before and after physically relocating each installation. The runs use MRI 3.3.12 on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor, 64-bit machine words and a recorded 20.0 host-load admission ceiling. The archive retains complete gems, extracted packages, receipts, installed inventories, execution records and both producer and verifier source closures. RubyGems remains a trusted part of the selected interpreter toolchain. Hosted glibc 2.38 release-floor acceptance remains assigned to the dedicated workflow. Constructor dispatch and peak memory are unmeasured.",
